{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":246299,"duration_api_ms":235808,"num_turns":38,"result":"All clean. Here is the ExecutionPayload:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"change_summary\": \"Improved `check_strictly_increasing` error reporting in invariants.rs by adding a new `OrderingViolation` variant to `SimError` that carries both the lower and upper field names and values. Previously, the error only reported the upper field (e.g., `InvariantViolation { field: \\\"shrimp_params.optimal_temp_max_c\\\", value: 30.0 }`) without mentioning the lower bound that caused the conflict. Now the error is `OrderingViolation { lower_field: \\\"shrimp_params.optimal_temp_min_c\\\", lower_value: 33.0, upper_field: \\\"shrimp_params.optimal_temp_max_c\\\", upper_value: 30.0 }` with a message like \\\"`shrimp_params.optimal_temp_min_c` (33) must be less than `shrimp_params.optimal_temp_max_c` (30)\\\". Updated all 3 call sites in invariants.rs to pass both field names, updated the API error handler to map the new variant to INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, and updated the save_load.rs test that asserts on the exact error. Also fixed two pre-existing compile issues in substrate.rs (changed `colonizable_area_factor(self)` to `&self` and added `Copy` derive to `SubstrateKind`) that were blocking workspace compilation.\",\n  \"outstanding_risks\": [\n    \"Pre-existing compile errors in tank_data/src/presets.rs (missing ParamMetaPreset impl for ProcessParamsPreset) block workspace-wide `cargo clippy --all-targets` — unrelated to this task, from another task's incomplete work\"\n  ],\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Read check_strictly_increasing in invariants.rs:398-412 and SimError::InvariantViolation in actions.rs:65-66 to understand the current error shape\",\n      \"order\": 1,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Surveyed all InvariantViolation match sites (error.rs, save_load.rs, validation.rs) to assess blast radius of